// Generated by scripts/api-docs.mjs from docs/API.md. Do not edit.
export const API_DOCS_HTML = "<h1 id=\"the-organization-api\">The organization API</h1>\n<p>For an organization's own scripts: HR syncs, offboarding tools, log collectors. Owners create keys on the organization's <strong>Settings</strong> page. A key is shown once; 2earl keeps only its SHA-256.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Base URL:</strong> <code>https://login.2earl.com/api/v1</code></li><li><strong>Authentication:</strong> <code>Authorization: Bearer 2earl_…</code></li><li><strong>Access:</strong> a <em>read</em> key reads; a <em>read and write</em> key also changes members.</li><li><strong>Format:</strong> JSON. Lists are <code>{ &quot;data&quot;: [...] }</code>. Errors are <code>{ &quot;error&quot;: &quot;code&quot;, &quot;message&quot;: &quot;…&quot; }</code> with a 4xx status.</li><li><strong>Limits:</strong> up to 5 keys per organization; requests are rate-limited per network address (<code>429</code>).</li><li><strong>Owners:</strong> the API never acts on them. Change owners in 2earl.</li><li><strong>Changes are pushed</strong> by the audit stream (Activity → Stream), not by polling.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"read\">Read</h2>\n<h3 id=\"get-members\"><code>GET /members</code></h3>\n<pre><code>{\n  &quot;data&quot;: [\n    {\n      &quot;id&quot;: &quot;6b1c…&quot;,\n      &quot;email&quot;: &quot;ada@example.com&quot;,\n      &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Ada Lovelace&quot;,\n      &quot;role&quot;: &quot;owner&quot;,\n      &quot;managed&quot;: true,\n      &quot;deactivated&quot;: false,\n      &quot;role_from_directory&quot;: false,\n      &quot;joined_at&quot;: &quot;2026-11-14T08:10:00.000Z&quot;\n    }\n  ]\n}</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"get-domains\"><code>GET /domains</code></h3>\n<pre><code>{ &quot;data&quot;: [{ &quot;domain&quot;: &quot;example.com&quot;, &quot;verified&quot;: true, &quot;managed&quot;: true }] }</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"get-audit\"><code>GET /audit</code></h3>\n<p>The organization's audit log, <strong>oldest first</strong>, from the last 90 days: everything that names the organization, and everything the accounts it manages did.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"log\"><thead><tr><th>Query</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>since</code></td><td>ISO 8601 time: events at or after it</td></tr><tr><td><code>cursor</code></td><td><code>next_cursor</code> from the previous page: events after it</td></tr><tr><td><code>limit</code></td><td>1 to 100 (default 100)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<pre><code>{\n  &quot;data&quot;: [\n    {\n      &quot;id&quot;: &quot;…&quot;,\n      &quot;time&quot;: &quot;2026-11-14T08:12:31.000Z&quot;,\n      &quot;event&quot;: &quot;login.succeeded&quot;,\n      &quot;actor&quot;: { &quot;id&quot;: &quot;6b1c…&quot;, &quot;email&quot;: &quot;ada@example.com&quot; },\n      &quot;target&quot;: null,\n      &quot;client_id&quot;: null,\n      &quot;ip_prefix&quot;: &quot;203.0.113.0/24&quot;,\n      &quot;detail&quot;: { &quot;method&quot;: &quot;oidc&quot; }\n    }\n  ],\n  &quot;next_cursor&quot;: &quot;1794643951.Zx8…&quot;\n}</code></pre>\n<p>To follow the log, store <code>next_cursor</code> and ask again with it; with no new events the same cursor comes back. Events of the last few seconds appear on the next call.</p>\n<h2 id=\"write-read-and-write-keys\">Write (read-and-write keys)</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"log\"><thead><tr><th>Request</th><th>Body</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POST /members/{id}/role</code></td><td><code>{ &quot;role&quot;: &quot;admin&quot; }</code> or <code>&quot;member&quot;</code></td><td>Changes the role. <code>409 directory</code> when the directory decides it (a group marked admin)</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /members/{id}/deactivate</code></td><td>none</td><td>A managed account can't sign in; sessions and app access end. <code>409 not_managed</code> otherwise</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /members/{id}/reactivate</code></td><td>none</td><td>Lifts the organization's deactivation</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /members/{id}/sign-out</code></td><td>none</td><td>Signs a managed account out everywhere: sessions and app access end, the account stays active. <code>409 not_managed</code> otherwise</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /members/{id}/remove</code></td><td>none</td><td>Removes a member the organization doesn't manage. <code>409 managed</code> for managed accounts: deactivate them</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Every change is in the organization's activity, with <code>&quot;via&quot;: &quot;api&quot;</code> and the key's ID.</p>\n<h2 id=\"directory-sync-scim-2-0\">Directory sync (SCIM 2.0)</h2>\n<p>Microsoft Entra ID, Okta and other directories provision people and groups into the organization. Owners create a token on <strong>Domains &amp; SSO</strong>, after verifying a domain.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Base URL:</strong> <code>https://login.2earl.com/scim/v2</code></li><li><strong>Authentication:</strong> <code>Authorization: Bearer scim_…</code></li><li><strong>Resources:</strong> <code>Users</code> and <code>Groups</code>: create, read, list, replace, patch, delete. <code>PATCH</code> takes the shapes Entra ID and Okta send, operation names in any case.</li><li><strong>Filters:</strong> <code>userName eq</code>, <code>externalId eq</code> (users); <code>displayName eq</code>, <code>externalId eq</code> (groups). <code>excludedAttributes=members</code> on groups.</li><li><strong>Discovery:</strong> <code>ServiceProviderConfig</code>, <code>ResourceTypes</code>, <code>Schemas</code>.</li><li><strong>Not supported:</strong> bulk, sorting, ETags, soft delete.</li></ul>\n<p>At a domain the organization manages, provisioning creates the 2earl account; <code>active: false</code> deactivates it; <code>DELETE</code> deactivates it at once and deletes it 30 days later unless it is reactivated first. Groups can be marked admin on <strong>Domains &amp; SSO</strong>: their members become admins.</p>";
